the batman is the latest take on one of  the most recognizable superheroes of all  time even the most offhand line in the  film reveals more about the character  than you might think wanna know more  keep watching  i'm vengeance  those two words spotlighted in the  trailer had already become something of  a viral sensation on social media before  the film was released similar to a  familiar line from tim burton's take on  the caped crusader  now you want to get nuts come on let's  get nuts but what's interesting is that  if you search  i'm vengeance on twitter many people  have embraced it in a way that pokes fun  at batman's constant brooding and  self-seriousness which largely mirrors  what happens in the film although batman  doesn't say the line in the presence of  any of the film's main characters that  doesn't stop catwoman from teasing him  about it a few others do as well  treating his declaration like an  embarrassing rage against the machine  lyric he once scribbled in their  yearbook selena kyle teases him at one  point saying come on vengeance obviously  certain elements are intrinsic in the  batman character his parents were  murdered and he has since spent his days  and nights training and planning to  become the ultimate crime deterrent a  big part of his power is the fear he  instills in gotham's criminals so if  there's anyone who could credibly utter  a line like i'm vengeance with complete  sincerity it would be the batman but at  the same time pattinson's batman is just  beginning to come to grips with the  cause and effect his presence has  created in gotham the crime is  relentless the villains are increasingly  more dynamic and his nightly efforts  don't seem to be making much of a dent  overall there's a sense of mere mockery  throughout the batman with characters  like riddler penguin and carmine falcone  treating their adversary's sincerity as  if it's a shortcoming  you got a lot of cats everything about  strength  it's a line spoken coily by selena kyle  in response to batman's less than  genuine observation it also sums up this  take on the character nearly every  action we see from this catwoman is  motivated by the welfare or memory of  someone else she's relentlessly  compassionate toward the vulnerable just  as you'd take in a stray cat and give it  the love it needs to grow however her  biggest motivation is her mission to  save her friend who has gone missing but  like batman she always has the memory of  her murdered mother colouring her  actions then of course there's batman  himself another stray that selena often  pushes cheers up and looks after take a  look at the scene where selena agrees to  wear special contact lenses that  broadcast a video signal to work at the  44 below club hidden within penguin's  iceberg lounge clearly she hates being  an informant for batman but she's  willing to risk her life to help out the  bat and hopefully get some information  on the missing girl's whereabouts in  some ways this take on catwoman might be  the most purely good one fans have seen  in a film sure she technically retains  the skills of a cat burglar but she uses  them to get back stolen passports rather  than steal family jewels arguably she's  every bit the hero the batman is and  unless you're willing to bring up halle  berry's catwoman zoe kravitz's take on  the character is the kindest catwoman  we've seen  the line is sure to get a giggle from  viewers and isn't that what the riddler  is all about that's too delicious i even  gave you a tip off and keep in mind  moviegoers haven't seen a cinematic take  on this character since jim carrey in  1995's batman forever more than anyone  else in batman's rogues gallery the man  typically known as edward nigma seems  made for these times the modern world is  filled with mind games fake news  anonymous troublemakers and other  touchstones the riddler once manipulated  with a pen and piece of paper this is  the perfect opportunity to update the  character into something more  threatening and less cartoonish and the  batman leans into that say hello to my  followers we're live he says at one  point kicking off a live stream with the  intention of holding the district  attorney accountable for his perceived  shortcomings they are here to watch our  little trial the riddler's creepy new  mask off-kilter glasses and defection  for duct tape result in a threatening  new look that no green leotard could  approach his grainy hostage videos and  mocking riddles work perfectly alongside  the user comments in the corners of the  frame riddler uses the tools of social  media to create a formidable army that  mimics him in appearance and technique  while the christopher nolan movies and  the snyder verse both used modern tech  to depict threats to batman neither of  them thought to do so via the riddler  now the character has been reimagined as  a jigsaw-like manipulator for the 21st  century  the potential for further development of  this incarnation of batman's foe and his  followers seems rife with potential  this line comes at a key point in the  film as bruce wayne continues to cling  to any loose string he can find of his  core principles he struggles as gotham  remains a city under siege and a rising  pile of bodies around him serves as  nagging indications he may be fighting a  losing battle carmine falcone one of the  most despicable puppeteers in gotham  solicits the line when he approaches  wayne and tries to bond with him your  father saved my life says the gangster  explaining that thomas wayne once tended  to him you think that doesn't mean  something dismissing the moment as  inconsequential bruce wayne tells  falcone his father did it out of  obligation not friendship that means he  took the hippocratic oath he says what  you're witnessing here is the final  moments of bruce wayne's naive view of  the way the world works in almost every  incarnation of batman thomas and martha  wayne are hugely powerful hugely beloved  characters senselessly gunned down they  are perfect martyrs for batman to avenge  but not in the batman instead further  revelations are to come about how thomas  and martha rose to power silenced their  critics and hid their secrets in short  thomas was far from a noble doctor who  treated everyone equally as the line  becomes blurred between carmine falcone  and thomas wayne it eats away at the  very foundation of the batman mission  could it be that thomas wayne wouldn't  simply help someone out of  professionalism and duty could it be  that falcone was a friend  for all his fancy talk and machiavellian  mind games falcone is just another  homicidal thug this becomes evident in  the final scenes involving the character  when he's confronted by selena their  struggle leads to him nearly strangling  her both bruce wayne and selena kyle  have significant backstories involving  dead parents and their involvement with  the movie's lead gangster falcone  however is a relatively recent creation  in the batman universe he made his debut  in a 1987 comic and although his  criminal activity has often been a  driving force behind gotham's sorry  state this is perhaps the most  influential we've ever seen the  character in essence without falcone  there likely wouldn't be a batman or a  catwoman but during a far more primal  moment falcone tells catwoman you made  me do this just like your mother as he  tries to choke her to death this  confession that he did in fact kill  maria kyle should bring closure for  selena on some level though she's not  able to appreciate it until falcone is  finally knocked off her and arrested  where does selena go from here like  several of the other main characters in  the batman she is essentially a grown  orphan grappling with demons and ghosts  she cannot ignore the last time we see  selena her storyline is resolved she has  no one left to be with and she's heading  off on her motorcycle to start a new  life now it seems she's the stray check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about the  batman are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

